<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prabuty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Riesenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prabuty, in German Riesenburg, is a small town in the Pomeranian Voivodeship of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its castle was the residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Pomesania, while their cathedral stood at nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwidzyn">Marienwerder</a>. The town passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a> in the 16th century and to Poland in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prabuty.jpg" alt="Prabuty" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MOs810 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prabuty_market_square_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
